---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site-config';
import { SITES } from '../../lib/sites';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd, productJsonLd } from '../../lib/seo';

const canonical = `${SITES.main}/products/hookah-charcoal/`;
const jsonLd = [
  breadcrumbJsonLd([
    { name: 'Home', url: `${SITES.main}/` },
    { name: 'Products', url: `${SITES.main}/products/` },
    { name: 'Hookah Charcoal', url: canonical },
  ]),
  productJsonLd({
    id: canonical,
    name: 'Hookah Charcoal',
    description: 'Hookah charcoal — natural coconut shell cubes and the FireMax bamboo/fruitwood range, supplier-declared.',
    category: 'Charcoal fuel',
    properties: [{ name: 'Raw material', value: 'Coconut shell / bamboo / fruitwood' }, { name: 'Size', value: '25–27 mm cubes; bars; 33 mm tablets' }, { name: 'Ignition', value: '8–12 min natural; 15–50 s instant-light' }, { name: 'Burning time', value: '45 min – 3 h depending on format' }],
  }),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  site={site}
  title="Hookah / Shisha Charcoal"
  description="Cube and flat hookah charcoal in 25mm, 26mm and 27mm sizes. Category overview — sizes, ash, burn time and ignition considerations for hookah buyers."
  canonical={canonical}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Products', url: '/products/' },
    { name: 'Hookah Charcoal', url: '/products/hookah-charcoal/' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="page-title-split container">
    <div>
      <h1>Hookah / Shisha Charcoal</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Cube and flat charcoal sized for hookah and shisha. The most common cube sizes are 25mm, 26mm
        and 27mm — the size choice affects heat output, burn time and how the charcoal fits the bowl.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="page-title-media">
      <img src="/images/product-hookah.webp" alt="Uniform hookah charcoal cubes with steel tongs on an aluminium tray — conceptual illustration" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Sizes</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Size</th><th>Typical Use</th><th>Buyer Consideration</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>25mm cube</td><td>Standard hookah sessions</td><td>Moderate heat and burn time; a common default.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>26mm cube</td><td>Standard hookah sessions</td><td>Slightly higher heat and longer burn than 25mm.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>27mm cube</td><td>Longer sessions / larger bowls</td><td>Higher heat output; fewer pieces needed.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="meta-line">
        Size naming reflects nominal cube edge length. Actual dimensions and dimensional tolerance are
        confirmed per product and reported in the product database — never assumed.
      </p>

      <h2>What to Evaluate</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Ash content</strong> — lower ash means less residue and cleaner smoking.</li>
          <li><strong>Burning time</strong> — how long a cube sustains usable heat.</li>
          <li><strong>Odor</strong> — neutral odor is preferred for hookah; charcoal should not add taste.</li>
          <li><strong>Ignition</strong> — time to full glow and consistency across a batch.</li>
          <li><strong>Spark level</strong> — low sparking is preferred for safety and clean sessions.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="callout-pending">
        <span class="callout-title">Data pending — supplier verification in progress</span>
        <p>
          Verified product entries for hookah charcoal are added to the product database after supplier
          verification. We do not publish unverified specifications.
        </p>
        <p><a href={`${SITES.data}/products/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Product Database →</a></p>
      </div>

      <h2>Specification Context</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          One product record in the database carries declared values for hookah charcoal — the
          25&nbsp;mm natural coconut shell cube. The figures below are reproduced for context and
          are <strong>supplier-declared, not independently verified by Charcoal Hub</strong>.
          The 26&nbsp;mm and 27&nbsp;mm records currently carry size-class data only (pieces per
          kilogram); no batch specification values are published for those sizes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Declared value</th><th>Method cited</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Fixed carbon</td><td>≥ 80%</td><td>ASTM D3172</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Volatile matter</td><td>≤ 12%</td><td>ASTM D3175</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ash content</td><td>≤ 3.5% (typical 3.0%)</td><td>ASTM D3174</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Moisture</td><td>≤ 5%</td><td>ASTM D3173</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sulphur</td><td>≤ 0.1%</td><td>ASTM D4239</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Burning time</td><td>~60 min (claims up to 120 min)</td><td>Condition-dependent — no universal standard</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ignition time</td><td>8–12 min</td><td>Supplier-declared</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="meta-line">
        Source: public supplier listing (bbqoncharcoal.com 25&nbsp;mm product page), captured
        2026-10-07. Supplier-declared — not independently verified by Charcoal Hub.
      </p>

      <h2>FireMax Product Range</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The FireMax datasheet (provided 2026-10-10) adds four hookah product records to the
          database — all <strong>supplier-declared</strong>, none independently tested:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>FireMax SL470</strong> — 4 × 4 × 3 cm bamboo cube, 2–3 h burn, ignition 9–10 min</li>
          <li><strong>FireMax C25</strong> — 25 mm bamboo cube, 90–120 min burn, 7,500 J</li>
          <li><strong>FireMax SI87</strong> — 90 × 25 × 12 mm silver bar, ignition 35–45 s</li>
          <li><strong>FireMax RB33</strong> — 33 mm instant-light tablet, ignition 15–50 s, 45–70 min burn</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <a href={`${SITES.data}/products/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">View records in the Product Database →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="page-title-media" style="max-width:640px;margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <img src="/images/firemax-rb33.webp" alt="Instant-light charcoal tablets on a stone tray, one lit — conceptual illustration" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" />
      </div>

      <h2>Buyer Checklist</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Method and basis.</strong> Confirm which method produced each figure and whether it is dry or as-received.</li>
          <li><strong>Batch linkage.</strong> Ask which batch, sample and date each number describes.</li>
          <li><strong>Raw report.</strong> Request the laboratory report, not a summary PDF.</li>
          <li><strong>Moisture at origin.</strong> Check moisture at origin and on arrival — hookah charcoal is hygroscopic.</li>
          <li><strong>Size and tolerance.</strong> Confirm the nominal cube size and tolerance; verify with calipers on a sample.</li>
          <li><strong>Odour neutrality.</strong> Assess odour on a blind sample in your own bowl — this is a session test, not a datasheet line.</li>
          <li><strong>Acceptance clause.</strong> Agree sampling and the remedy for an out-of-spec arrival in the purchase order.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Verification Status</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          No hookah charcoal product has yet been independently verified by Charcoal Hub. Published
          figures are supplier-declared and labelled as such. Verified test reports will be published
          on the <a href={`${SITES.testing}/reports/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">testing sub-site</a>
          as they become attributable.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Related</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <a class="card" href={`${SITES.data}/products/25mm-natural-coconut-shell-hookah-charcoal/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <h3>25 mm product record <span class="badge badge-muted">data</span></h3>
          <p>Supplier-declared specification values with source and status.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={`${SITES.data}/specifications/burning-time/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <h3>Burning time methodology <span class="badge badge-muted">data</span></h3>
          <p>Why burn time has no universal standard and how to compare claims.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={`${SITES.testing}/tests/burning-time/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <h3>Test methodology <span class="badge badge-muted">testing</span></h3>
          <p>How burn time is assessed under defined, configuration-specific protocols.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={`${SITES.knowledge}/knowledge/how-to-choose-hookah-charcoal/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <h3>How to choose <span class="badge badge-muted">knowledge</span></h3>
          <p>A buyer decision framework for hookah charcoal.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={`${SITES.knowledge}/knowledge/25mm-vs-26mm-charcoal/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <h3>25 mm vs 26 mm <span class="badge badge-muted">knowledge</span></h3>
          <p>What the size difference actually changes in a session.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/request-sample/">
          <h3>Request samples</h3>
          <p>Test a batch in your own hardware before ordering.</p>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-banner">
        <h2>Sourcing hookah charcoal?</h2>
        <p>Tell us your size, quantity and destination port.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Request a Quote →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/request-sample/" style="margin-left:0.5rem;">Request Samples →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
